    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras on this May 28th slate, **Colt Keith** stands as our premier play with a 68.51 efficiency score, bolstered significantly by a plus-matchup against Rodriguez. His role atop the lineup against a high-xERA starter provides the perfect storm of counting stat opportunity and run-scoring potential. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** also profiles as an elite play at 62.47; despite the daunting challenge of facing Skenes, the combination of his leadoff spot, a favorable wind-out condition, and an aggressive platoon edge against the right-handed starter keeps his ceiling high for stolen base contributions. Similarly, **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) provides essential stability at shortstop, capitalizing on a weak opposing arm in Rojas to anchor the middle of our order.\n\nWe are forced into a difficult roster management scenario due to the heavy density of off-days for our core stars like **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich**, who are all unavailable today. Among those on the active roster, **Caleb Durbin** represents our most precarious start at a 40.67 score. While his speed remains vital to our strategy, the matchup against the elite Chris Sale, combined with a 35% rain risk and a low-leverage #9 lineup slot, nearly forced him to the bench. We are proceeding with **Durbin** to hunt for potential steals, but he remains a candidate for early substitution if the weather worsens or he struggles against Sale\u2019s command. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (57.01) offers a solid floor despite facing a tough opponent in Eovaldi, as his elite .422 xwOBA remains too impactful to sit, even when the underlying matchup metrics suggest a slight regression from his usual production. **Dillon Dingler** (53.73) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.93) round out our lineup, with **Okamoto** looking particularly poised to produce provided his spot in the lineup holds firm at #5.",
